        "original_id": "d76cb596-94ab-5ac5-98e3-aa78d17ba0d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: HMS Scipion\n- People: Scipio Africanus\n- Organizations: British Royal Navy\n- Concepts: French term for Roman names\n\nFacts:\n- Publius Cornelius Scipio Africanus lived from 236 BC to 183 BC.\n- Publius Cornelius Scipio Africanus was also known as Scipio the African, Scipio Africanus-Major, Scipio Africanus the Elder, and Scipio the Great.\n- Publius Cornelius Scipio Africanus was a Roman general and later consul.\n- Publius Cornelius Scipio Africanus is often regarded as one of the greatest generals and military strategists of all time.\n- Two ships of the British Royal Navy have borne the name HMS Scipion.\n- The name HMS Scipion uses the French term for the Roman general Scipio Africanus.",
